      "body": "## Motivation\n\nRegistering an HTTP worker whose `/health` endpoint requires authentication fails even when the registration request includes the correct `api_key`. The initial connection detection probe omits the key, while periodic HTTP health checks already send it.\n\nThis affects workers behind authentication proxies or middleware. Stock SGLang health endpoints do not require authentication.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Pass the configured worker API key to the initial HTTP `/health` probe as a Bearer token.\n- Preserve unauthenticated requests when no worker key is configured.\n- Add regression coverage for valid, missing, and incorrect worker credentials, plus registration-time probing without a worker key.\n- Document authentication for initial and periodic HTTP health checks.\n\nInference authentication, BYOK behavior, and circuit-breaker policies are outside this change.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Confirmed the authenticated regression test fails with HTTP 401 on the pre-fix code and passes with this change.\n- `cargo +1.90 test`: passed.\n- `cargo +nightly fmt -- --check`: passed.\n- `pre-commit run --all-files`: passed.\n\nThese are local verification results; GitHub Actions results remain to be verified.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable: this change does not affect model computation or outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: this change only adds authentication to the registration-time health probe.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #38417160343](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38417160343)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38417160329](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38417160329)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
